    {
      "bbox": [
        171,
        780,
        1680,
        1190
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "The provisions of section 5 of the Interim Order, relating to the institution and observance of grievance procedures, are hereby incorporated in and made a part of this order, with the following changes and additions:\n\nAny individual employee may present his own grievance either personally or through an appropriate representative or an organization of which he is a member and have such grievance adjusted: Provided, however, that where a majority representative has been selected as the bargaining agent for the unit of which the employee is a part, the grievance may be presented and processed either by such bargaining agent or by the employee as an individual, but not through any minority organization.",
